=====================================
FOLDER: energies
SYSTEM: MareNostrum 5 — glogin2
CREATED: 01/10/2026
UPDATED: 07/10/2026
PURPOSE: Converts the pH speciation of ../speciation into an observable: a
         Boltzmann-weighted effective activation free energy and Eyring rate
         constant for pyrophosphate hydrolysis as a function of pH, with and
         without Mg(II), compared against Wolfenden's experimental curve.
=====================================

01/10/2026

o This folder is the second half of the RESULTS analysis. '../speciation' answers
  "which species exist at which pH"; this folder answers "what barrier does the
  solution as a whole present at that pH". There is no MD and no DFT here, only
  post-processing of a speciation curve plus a table of per-species barriers.

o The model is in 'delta_G.py'. It reads two files. 'energies.txt' is a single row
  of eight activation free energies in kcal/mol, one per species, with the species
  names in the header comment: 'pp hpp h2pp h3pp h4pp mgpp mghpp mg2pp'. The second
  file is a 'concentrations_vs_pH_<Mg>_<PP>.dat' copied over from the matching
  '../speciation' run. The script converts the concentrations into mole fractions
  within a chosen group of species, Boltzmann-weights exp(-E/RT) by those fractions,
  and takes -RT ln of the sum to get an effective barrier per pH point. It then
  applies Eyring with A = kB*T/h to get a rate constant. Constants are
  R = 1.987e-3 kcal/(mol*K) and T = 298 K (298.15 K in some copies).

o Invocation is 'python3 delta_G.py <energy_filename> <concentration_filename>'.
  The outputs written next to it are 'DeltaG_resume.txt' (pH, non-catalyzed dG,
  non-catalyzed k, catalyzed dG, catalyzed k), 'pp_K_per_species.txt' and
  'mg_K_per_species.txt' (per-species rate constants, not pH-resolved),
  'Energy_vs_pH.png' and 'K_vs_pH.png'. Some folders also carry 'ratios_pp.txt',
  'ratios_mg.txt' and 'boltzmann_coeff' files, which are the intermediate mole
  fractions and weights from a variant of the script.

o Subfolder naming follows '../speciation': 'MMMM_PPPP' with the two four-digit
  blocks the total Mg and total pyrophosphate in millimolar, so '0010_0050' is
  total Mg = 0.010 M and total PP = 0.050 M. Three older folders break that
  convention and use a loose decimal spelling instead: '01_002', '03_03' and
  '1_0002'. 'wolfenden_case' is not a concentration at all, it is the composition
  chosen to line up with the experimental reference.

o IMPORTANT, and the first thing to check before comparing any two subfolders:
  these runs are NOT all the same calculation. They fall into two generations that
  differ both in the input barriers and in the definition of the "catalyzed"
  curve, and nothing in the folder names signals which is which.

    Old generation -- 'energies.txt' has hpp = 29.0 and h3pp = 23.5, and
    'catalyzed' is the three magnesium complexes only, ["mgpp","mghpp","mg2pp"].
    Folders: '0001_0120', '0020_0050', '01_002', '03_03', '1_0002'.
    Outputs dated 06/08/2026 and 19/08/2026, 'DeltaG_resume.txt' is 16 KB.

    New generation -- 'energies.txt' has hpp = 31.18 and h3pp = 23.75, and
    'catalyzed' is ALL eight species, i.e. the whole solution including the
    protonation ladder, not just the Mg complexes. Folders: '0010_0010',
    '0010_0020', '0010_0050', '0050_0100'. Outputs dated 29/08/2026 and
    31/08/2026, 'DeltaG_resume.txt' is 25 KB.

    'wolfenden_case' uses the new-generation grouping but its own 'energies.txt'
    again (hpp = 31.2), and its output is dated 20/09/2026.

o The consequence of the grouping change is worth spelling out, because it looks
  like a bug when it is not. In the new generation the two columns of
  'DeltaG_resume.txt' agree to several decimal places at low pH. That is expected:
  the "catalyzed" group now contains the same five protonated species as the
  "non-catalyzed" group, and below pH ~4 those dominate both averages, so the two
  curves must coincide there. The curves are meant to be read as "Mg-free solution"
  versus "solution with Mg present", not as "uncatalyzed path" versus "catalyzed
  path". Under the old grouping the second column was the Mg-complex subensemble
  renormalized to itself, which is a different quantity and is not comparable.

o Second trap: the 'delta_G.py' sitting at the top of this folder is the OLD
  generation. It is not the script that produced the new-generation subfolders.
  Every subfolder keeps its own frozen copy of the script it was actually run with,
  and those copies differ from the top-level one in all ten cases. Re-running the
  top-level script will not reproduce '0010_0050'. Always use the copy inside the
  subfolder.

o 'concentrations_vs_pH_0.001_0.12.dat' at the top level is a loose speciation curve
  for 0.001 M Mg / 0.120 M PP, the input of the '0001_0120' run.

o 'wolfenden_case' additionally holds 'wolfend_data.txt', two columns of pH and
  experimental dG covering pH 5 to 12, read by its script and overlaid on the
  calculated curves. Its plots are the publication-style comparison: calculated
  Mg-free, experimental Mg-free, and calculated with Mg, plus a zoomed
  'Energy_vs_pH_snippet.png' restricted to pH 7-12.

o Not verified in this pass: where the per-species barriers in 'energies.txt' come
  from. They are entered by hand and are presumably the PMF/US results from
  '../../LFER/LFER_3_mg2', but no provenance file ties a given number to a given
  WHAM output. Anyone revising the barriers should record that mapping.

07/10/2026

o Provenance of 'energies.txt', which the 01/10 entry left open: Elia wrote these
  barrier tables by hand and copied them into each subfolder manually. No script in
  this tree generates them, so there is no pipeline to re-run and no mapping to a WHAM
  output to recover. If a barrier changes, the file has to be edited by hand again,
  and the two generations documented above are the record of that having happened.
